### What does it mean to find employees sharing a birthday month?

Sharing a birthday month means two or more employees have a birth date in the same calendar month, regardless of the day or year. The `java.time.Month` enum (JANUARY through DECEMBER) provides the grouping key. Grouping by `Month` and then filtering for groups with more than one member identifies the months where multiple employees share birthdays.

This is a classic group-then-filter pattern that appears frequently in stream interview questions.

### How do you implement it with streams?

The solution has three parts: guard nulls, group by month, and filter for shared months.

```java
package com.bank.hr;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.time.Month;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class SharedBirthdayMonth {

    record Employee(String id, String name, LocalDate birthDate,
                    String department, BigDecimal salary) {}

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Employee> staff = List.of(
            new Employee("SAV2001", "Rajesh",  LocalDate.of(1989, 1, 22), "TRADING",    new BigDecimal("1800000")),
            new Employee("SAV2002", "Priya",   LocalDate.of(1995, 1, 5),  "RISK",       new BigDecimal("1200000")),
            new Employee("SAV2003", "Amit",    LocalDate.of(1990, 3, 15), "COMPLIANCE", new BigDecimal("900000")),
            new Employee("SAV2004", "Kavita",  LocalDate.of(1985, 7, 10), "OPERATIONS", new BigDecimal("1100000")),
            new Employee("SAV2005", "Meera",   LocalDate.of(1986, 7, 25), "TRADING",    new BigDecimal("1500000")),
            new Employee("SAV2006", "Ananya",  LocalDate.of(1992, 5, 8),  "RISK",       new BigDecimal("1050000"))
        );

        // Step 1: Group by birth month, guarding nulls
        Map<Month, List<Employee>> byMonth = staff.stream()
            .filter(e -> e.birthDate() != null)
            .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(e -> e.birthDate().getMonth()));

        // Step 2: Keep only months with 2+ employees
        Map<Month, List<Employee>> shared = byMonth.entrySet().stream()
            .filter(entry -> entry.getValue().size() > 1)
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(
                Map.Entry::getKey, Map.Entry::getValue,
                (a, b) -> a, TreeMap::new));  // TreeMap for chronological order

        // Step 3: Display
        shared.forEach((month, employees) -> {
            System.out.println(month + ":");
            employees.forEach(e -> System.out.println(
                "  " + e.name() + " (" + e.birthDate() + ")"));
        });
    }
}
```

```text
JANUARY:
  Rajesh (1989-01-22)
  Priya (1995-01-05)
JULY:
  Kavita (1985-07-10)
  Meera (1986-07-25)
```

### How do you get a flat list of employees who share a month?

If you need a single `List<Employee>` rather than the grouped map, use `flatMap` on the filtered groups.

```java
List<Employee> sharingEmployees = shared.values().stream()
    .flatMap(Collection::stream)
    .toList();

System.out.println("Employees sharing a birthday month: " + sharingEmployees.size());
```

```text
Employees sharing a birthday month: 4
```

### How is grouping by Month different from grouping by MonthDay?

| Aspect | `Month` | `MonthDay` |
|---|---|---|
| Grouping key | Calendar month only (JANUARY) | Month + day (--01-22) |
| Matches | Same month, any day | Exact same month and day |
| Use case | Birthday month celebration | Exact birthday twins |
| Key type | `java.time.Month` enum | `java.time.MonthDay` |

```java
// Group by exact month-day for birthday twins
Map<java.time.MonthDay, List<Employee>> byMonthDay = staff.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.birthDate() != null)
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
        e -> java.time.MonthDay.from(e.birthDate())));
```

### What are common mistakes?

Mistake 1: Including months with only one employee.

```java
// WRONG: no filter, shows all months including singletons
byMonth.forEach((month, emps) -> {
    System.out.println(month + ": " + emps.size());
});

// CORRECT: filter for size > 1 to find actual sharing
Map<Month, List<Employee>> shared = byMonth.entrySet().stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getValue().size() > 1)
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Map.Entry::getKey, Map.Entry::getValue));
```

Mistake 2: Not guarding null birth dates.

```java
// WRONG: NullPointerException if birthDate is null
staff.stream().collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
    e -> e.birthDate().getMonth()));  // throws NPE

// CORRECT: filter nulls first
staff.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.birthDate() != null)
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(e -> e.birthDate().getMonth()));
```

### What about ordering the output chronologically?

The default `groupingBy` produces a `HashMap`, which has no guaranteed order. To get months in calendar order, use a `TreeMap` supplier.

```java
Map<Month, List<Employee>> byMonthOrdered = staff.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.birthDate() != null)
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
        e -> e.birthDate().getMonth(),
        TreeMap::new,
        Collectors.toList()));
// Keys iterate in natural Month enum order: JANUARY, FEBRUARY, ...
```

